  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Kustom Kombi-Weapon" id="8a14-512e-51e3-293a" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Nominate a target when the weapon is fired, and roll a D6 and an Artillery dice. Multiply the score on the D6 by 10: the result is the range of the attack in inches.
If the target is in range then it is automatically hit.
The number on the Artillery dice is the Strength of the attack.
Half the Artillery dice roll to determine the save modifier.
Any vehicle hit by the kombi-weapon will take a single hit with an armour penetration equal to the Strength of the attack plus a D6

If you roll a misfire on the Artillery dice, roll a D6:
1-3: Blows up - the mode using the weapon is killed
4-6: Misfire - May not fire this turn but may be used next turn as normal</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shokk Attack Gun" id="17aa-5f03-b0c8-9ef9" hidden="false" page="18-19" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Rules too long for this, see page 18 &amp; 19 in the Ork Codex for rules on using this weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Always Hits" id="d7aa-a360-b2d3-a3f1" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>A target fired at by a Gretchin Blunderbuss is hit automatically and no &quot;to hit&quot; roll is required</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Snotlings" id="3ad1-1359-987a-4083" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Snotlings are small and will have multiple on a single base. Treat it as a single large monster with several wounds and attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runtherdz" id="89f2-1343-924e-50a4" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Runtherdz act as champions for units of Snotlings and Gretchin. No other Ork may lead Snotlings and Gretchin because they consider it to be a waste of time</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Madmob" id="302f-d937-576d-d915" hidden="false" page="25" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Madboyz always fight as a single mob on their own, they cannot be led by any other Ork, nor can they benefit from the Leadership bonus of other Orks</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mad!" id="fa1a-f039-985a-0269" hidden="false" page="25" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Roll a D6 at the start of the game and constul the chart (Pg.25 Codex Orks). This establishes the maddness for the Madmob. The mob is subject to the psychology rule indicated from then on.
At the start of each subsequent turn the Ork player rolls a D6: On a 1-5 nothing happens and continues with its last roll. On a 6, you roll on the chart again to determine the maddness.
Should the Madmob be broken, then a new maddness is established as soon as it ralies.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Minders - Weirdboy" id="1dc8-c485-a2d0-14ec" hidden="false" page="26" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Must remain in base contact with the Weirdboy at all times. If they are killed, the Weirdboy must move to the nearest table edge as fast as possible. Once he leaves the battle he will not come back</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Minders - Warphead" id="99a2-75c5-5a50-95cd" hidden="false" page="26" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Must remain in base contact with the Weirdboy at all times. If they are killed, the Warphead will make a run move towards the biggest group of Orks he can find, trying to get within 12&quot; of the best source of Waaagh! power. 
In the psychic phase, a Warphead without any Minderz will always fire off a psychic power picked at random. If you have other WEirdboyz in your force you can only use psyhic powers from them after the Waprhead has used one of his powers. If you don&apos;t have enough warp cards to make the randomly chosen power work there is no further effect and you can play powers from other Weirdboyz freely.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Madboyz and Warpheads" id="2af2-7f97-7ba4-76ce" hidden="false" page="27" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Madboyz can take Leadership tests using the Warphead&apos;s Leadership of 8 if he is within 2&quot; of them, even though Madboyz can&apos;t normally benefit from another character&apos;s higher Leadership characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cyboar" id="526e-49e2-b785-8368" hidden="false" page="28" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>+2 save for the Ork (this includes the usual Cavalry save already)
-1 Leadership penalty at all times while riding a Warboar
+2 combat result modifier when charging
Once per game can inject Cyboar with chemicals gaining: D6+4 Movement and D4 attacks for the remainder of the turn. The movement bonus is not doubled if the Boarboy is charging or running. This can be done on your turn or the enemy turn</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warboar" id="a090-8c27-9a7b-511a" hidden="false" page="28" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>+2 save (this includes the usual Cavalry save already)
-1 Leadership penalty at all times while riding a Warboar
+2 combat result modifier when charging</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warboss" id="25c2-55ee-c98a-27a9" hidden="false" page="63" publicationId="4590-6ba9-5482-a1fa">
      <description>Any Ork units that have a model within 12&quot; of him  may use his Leadership when they take a Break or Panic test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ork Battle Standard" id="e802-5a9c-b7bc-c344" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Any Ork units that have a model within 12&quot; of the Battle Standard may re-roll the dice if they fail a Break Test</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ork Dreadnought Damage Table" id="f7f6-86e6-9534-e851" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1:  Legs
2: Left Arm*
3: Right Arm*
4-6: Body
*Roll a D6, 1-3, upper arm, 4-5, lower arm</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battlewagon Damage Table" id="1fb8-b263-77b9-bc2f" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1:  Wheel*
2-4: Hull
5-6: Passengers**
*Hit the closest wheel to the attacker
**Hit the passenger nearest the attacker. If a blast weapon, any models under the template are hit on a 4+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battlewagon" id="aced-192a-5f86-f22c" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>The Battlewagon can carry as many models as can fit or balance on the model. Any models that fall off when moving the model count as having fallen off in gameplay terms too and the normal rules apply for their damage. See Pg. 77 of the 40k Rulebook

Orks in the Battlewagon may use any weapons that they are carrying. The field of fire is based on the position of the individual Ork model within the vehicle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ork Field Artillery" id="4746-1263-96ff-a156" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Attacking Field Artillery:
If being shot, the artillery is considered to be a separate target from the crew. At short range, an enemy may select one of the crew or the weapon itself as the target. At long range, any shots are randomised between the weapon and any crew members.
If the crew is reduced to half strength, the weapon can only be fired on a 4+. 
If the weapon is hit, it is considered to have an armour value of 10. If penetrated the weapon is destroyed and crew slain.

Moving Field Artillery:
Can be moved 2&quot; per turn by crew. Cannot be moved and fired. 
Can be attached to a vehicle (if at least 1 crew memeber is alive) and moved with the vehicle. Can be unhitched if the vehicle stops and placed within 1&quot;, or unhitched while the vehicle is moving. If done while moving, it is unhitched D6&quot; in a random direction and a random facing from the point you unhitched. Work out collision damage as detailed in the vehicle rules if needed. Ram value is the same as an Ork Bike (S5, -2 save, D4 damage). The crew take an automatic hit wit ha Strength equal to the vehicle&apos;s speed -10.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Artillery Rules" id="15f3-31f2-768d-1112" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>All the field artillery rules are a full page of rules for each gun. Too much to put into Battlescribe without it becoming a huge amount of clutter. Please see the Ork Field Artillery section in the codex, pg.12</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Nobz Bike Damage Table" id="ca8d-7782-ec06-d480" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1-3: Crew*
4-6: Bike
*Hit the passenger nearest the attacker.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Nobz Bike" id="60c6-33e5-7c4d-6783" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>The bike has no weapons but the Nob riding it may fire any of his weapons in a 360° arc</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="War Buggy Damage Table" id="72b2-a435-bbf3-eefd" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1-3: Crew*
4-6: War Buggy
*Hit the passenger nearest the attacker.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ork Scorcher Damage Table" id="27e6-01f0-5f5f-530b" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1: Driver
2: Turret
3-5: Scorcher
6: Fuel Tank</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wartrukk Damage Table" id="a2a1-687e-84c1-9e22" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1-2: Wartrukk
3-6: Passengers*
*Hit the passenger nearest the attacker.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warbike Damage Table" id="e478-9c0d-4966-b20c" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1-3: Crew*
4-6: Bike
*Hit the passenger nearest the attacker.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mad Doc Grotsnik" id="ee38-630e-4b0b-972b" hidden="false" page="65" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Follows rules for Madboy
Not allowed to join or lead any mobs and must always remain on his own.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ghazghkull Waaagh!" id="58b2-c882-4683-0f8b" hidden="false" page="66" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Once per game Ghazghkull may call a Waaagh! at any time, even during the opponents turn. As soon as he calls the power of the Waaagh, any fleeing Ork models immediately rally. For the remainder of the turn and all of the following turn he is immune to any damage - he cannot be harmed in any way at all - and all Orks (including Ghazghkull himself) receive a +1 modifier in close combat</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Makari Battle Standard" id="96a7-c922-49f1-0f6b" hidden="false" page="66" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>2+ save which can never be modified for any reason, against any type of damage that he suffers for any reason

Must always remain within 2&quot; of Ghazghkull at all times</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Speed Freak" id="3cb3-5a27-43fd-2b75" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>+2 to the dice roll when rolling on the Bike Skid Turn table (Pg. 83 of Warhammer rulebook).
May not decrease his speed compared to a previous turn unless he takes and passes a Speed test first on a D6:
1-3: Slows down
4-5: Same speed as previous turn
6: Yaaaaaaaaaargh!: Vehicle accelerates to its max speed regardless of the players wish</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battle Cannon Recoil" id="3c42-2ff1-56b5-ba31" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>Wazdakka and his warbike are pushed D3&quot; directly backwards every time that the battle cannon is fired, and wil collide with any model or obstacle they hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wartrak Damage Table" id="77e9-013b-bb0a-8ed6" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46">
      <description>1-3: Crew*
4-6: Wartrak
*Hit the passenger nearest the attacker.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
