          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Doc&apos;s Tools" id="475a-95ab-3ce0-a668" hidden="false" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">A Painboy with a set of tools always counts as having two close combat weapons, and so always rolls an extra dice in close combat. If the Painboy wins a round of combat and inflicts at least 1 wound then the opponent is assumed to have been injected with a Syringe squig. The model is removed as a casualty even if they still have wounds remaining.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Cybork Body" id="f773-b0bb-55ca-b4d1" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8ed1-5e47-dd40-a9d1" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="71cc-8d0f-e5d9-1467" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="a7a6-8bf0-fcf9-e5d1" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="35"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Cybork Body" id="4f80-457b-9829-2770" hidden="false" page="46" publicationId="9f92-b7df-cf75-9a46" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">Increase Strength and Wounds by +2
In addition, if the Ork is hit by an attack then he is treated in the same way as a vehicle or Dreadnought with an armour value of 15. Roll for armour penetration as normal. If the attack equals the armour value, then the Ork is knocked over and may not move or shoot in his next turn while he stands up. If the attack beats the Ork&apos;s armour value, then he knocked over as above and suffers 1 wound for each point the attack beat the armour value by.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
